.TH XUR.STD.MEM 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.mem \- struct layout, binary conversion and page allocation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::mem;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::mem
provides size and alignment queries, binary conversion for structs
with a layout (see
.BR xur.std.reflect (7)),
and cross-platform memory page allocation for assembling and
executing machine code at runtime.
.SH LAYOUT FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B size_of::<T>() -> i64
The size in bytes of
.IR T .
.TP
.B align_of::<T>() -> i64
The alignment of
.IR T .
.TP
.B size_of_val(value) -> i64
The size in bytes of a struct value.
.TP
.B from_bytes::<T>(data) -> T
Read a struct of type
.I T
from the start of
.IR data .
.TP
.B to_bytes(value) -> bytes
Serialize a struct value to bytes.
.SH STRUCT METHODS
Every struct value also has:
.TP
.B value.to_bytes() -> bytes
Serialize the struct to bytes using its layout.
.TP
.B value.byte_size() -> i64
The struct's size in bytes.
.SH PAGE ALLOCATION
.TP
.B alloc_page(size) -> *u8
Allocate
.I size
bytes of read-write memory. Returns a raw pointer.
Uses
.B mmap
on Unix and
.B VirtualAlloc
on Windows.
.TP
.B protect(addr, size, mode)
Change page protection.
.I mode
is a
.B Protection
flags value (see below) or a string:
.BR \(dqr\(dq ,
.BR \(dqrw\(dq ,
.BR \(dqrx\(dq ,
or
.BR \(dqrwx\(dq .
.TP
.B write_bytes(addr, data)
Copy
.I data
(bytes) into memory at
.IR addr .
.TP
.B free_page(addr, size)
Free a page allocated with
.BR alloc_page .
.SH PROTECTION ENUM
.B mem::Protection
is a
.B #[repr(i64)]
bitwise flags enum:
.TP
.B Protection::Read \fR(1)
Allow reading.
.TP
.B Protection::Write \fR(2)
Allow writing.
.TP
.B Protection::Execute \fR(4)
Allow execution.
.PP
Flags are combined with
.BR | :
.PP
.RS
.nf
mem::Protection::Read | mem::Protection::Execute
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Struct layout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
use std::mem;
use std::io;

#[repr(C)]
struct Header { magic: u32, version: u16 }

fn main() {
    io::println("size: {}", mem::size_of::<Header>());
    let h = Header { magic: 0x5a4d, version: 1 };
    let data = h.to_bytes();
    io::println("bytes: {}", data.to_hex());
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Allocate, write, protect and call executable memory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
use std::mem;

fn main() {
    let page: *fn() = mem::alloc_page(4096);
    mem::write_bytes(page, code);
    mem::protect(page, 4096,
        mem::Protection::Read | mem::Protection::Execute);
    let result = page();
    mem::free_page(page, 4096);
}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.reflect (7),
.BR xur.std.bytes (7),
.BR xur.std.re (7)
